{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<section class="py-16 md:py-24 border-b border-base-300/50 bg-base-200/50 relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute top-10 left-10 w-72 h-72 bg-secondary/5 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10">
    <span class="badge badge-secondary badge-outline badge-sm mb-4 tracking-wider uppercase">Privacy</span>
    <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy <span class="text-secondary">Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="text-base-content/70 max-w-3xl">
      Last updated: 15 March 2026. This policy explains how Norstar Inline Hockey Club handles personal data in line with UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">1. Who we are</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            Norstar Inline Hockey Club (“we”, “us”, “our”) is the data controller for personal data processed through this website and our club administration processes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            For data protection queries, contact us via <a href="/contact" class="text-secondary hover:underline"> contact</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">2. Personal data we collect</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base-content/80">
            <li>Identity and contact details for parents/guardians and players where relevant.</li>
            <li>Club participation data, such as team registrations, attendance, and availability responses.</li>
            <li>Account data, including role-based access information for secure member areas.</li>
            <li>Communication data submitted through contact or account forms.</li>
            <li>Technical/security data (for example IP address and session-related information) required to keep the site secure.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">3. Why we process data and lawful bases</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">Under UK GDPR, we rely on one or more of the following lawful bases:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base-content/80">
            <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to deliver requested club services and manage membership activities.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — where we must comply with legal requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — to run, safeguard, and improve club operations and website security.</li>
            <li><strong>Consent</strong> — where required for optional processing activities.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">4. Children’s data</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            As a youth club, some processing relates to children. We aim to minimise data collection and process only what is necessary for participation, communication, and safeguarding administration.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">5. Cookies and website security</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            We use essential cookies or similar technologies to support secure sign-in, session management, and core website functionality. We do not use these essential technologies for advertising.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">6. How long we keep data</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            We retain personal data only for as long as needed for club operations, safeguarding context, legal requirements, and legitimate administrative needs. Data is deleted or anonymised when no longer necessary.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">7. Sharing and international transfers</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            We may share data with authorised staff/volunteers and trusted service providers that support club operations. We do not sell personal data. If data is transferred outside the UK, we use appropriate safeguards where required.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">8. Your rights</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">You may have rights under UK GDPR, including:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base-content/80">
            <li>Access to your personal data.</li>
            <li>Correction of inaccurate data.</li>
            <li>Erasure, restriction, or objection in certain circumstances.</li>
            <li>Data portability where applicable.</li>
            <li>Withdrawal of consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            You can contact us via <a href="/contact" class="text-secondary hover:underline">contact</a>. 
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 shadow-xl">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class="text-base-content/80">
            We may update this policy from time to time. Any updates will be posted on this page with the revised date.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
